dialogue trust_redmage_5
title: What the fire is for
trigger: Trust redmage level=5
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Red Mage sits by the cold fire pit with the dented tin open on one knee and a folded scrap of letter-paper on the other, read so often it has gone soft as cloth.
  * You kept what the tithe couldn't take. I said it then. I'd say it again. -> honoured_back
    if: FlagSet redmage:coal_honoured
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * You told me you were waiting to find out what that coal was for. Did you? -> asked_back
    if: FlagSet redmage:coal_asked
    do: AddTrust $with 6
  * I told you once to be careful with that tin. I was wrong to make it sound like a threat. -> warned_back
    if: FlagSet redmage:coal_warned
    do: AddTrust $with 7
  * News from the fens? -> news
    do: AddTrust $with 3

node honoured_back hero
  I told the coal, you know. That very night. It didn't say anything back, but it burned a bit taller. Sit down. There's news.
  -> letter

node asked_back hero
  I think so. I think tonight's the night I find out. Sit down. There's news.
  -> letter

node warned_back hero
  You weren't wrong. You were a commander with a camp full of wagons. And I never once set one alight, did I? Sit down. There's news.
  -> letter

node news hero
  From a cousin in Saltmoss who can barely spell, so it took a while to read. Sit down.
  -> letter

node letter hero
  My aunt sat by the cold hearth the way she always does. And then, out of nothing, she said my name. Asked where I'd gone. Nine years, Commander, and she never asked after anyone.
  -> hope

node hope commander
  The Red Mage turns the letter over, though the back is blank, and turns it again.
  * We said we'd try together, with the orb. When the road goes back past Saltmoss, we will. -> promised_kept
    if: FlagSet redmage:test_promised
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag redmage:thread_promise
  * I wouldn't let you try. I think I was afraid of what it would cost you. I'm sorry. -> refused_mended
    if: FlagSet redmage:test_refused
    do: AddTrust $with 10
    do: SetFlag redmage:thread_mended
  * You asked me to help you stop wanting to fix her. Maybe you don't have to stop. Maybe she's asking for you, not for a cure. -> questioned_kept
    if: FlagSet redmage:test_questioned
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag redmage:thread_asking
  * Then write back. Tell her where you've gone. -> write
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag redmage:thread_letter

node promised_kept hero
  You remembered. I wasn't sure you would. Then I'll stop counting the days and start counting the miles. That's a better kind of sum.
  -> coal

node refused_mended hero
  Afraid for me. Huh. Nobody's been afraid for me since I was small. I'm not sorry you said no. I'm glad you said that.
  -> coal

node questioned_kept hero
  Asking for me. Not waiting to be mended. Just asking where I'd gone. I hadn't let myself read it that way. I think you're right.
  -> coal

node write hero
  I will. I'll tell her I'm with a commander who stole the Choir's white wagon and talks to me like I'm worth answering. She'll think I've joined a circus.
  -> coal

node coal hero
  So. The coal. Nine years I've carried it, waiting for it to be for something. I think it's for tonight. I just don't know which way.
  -> choose

node choose commander
  The Red Mage holds the open tin out across the cold fire pit.
  * Light the camp fire with it. Her hearth can warm all of us now. -> campfire
    do: AddTrust $with 8
    do: SetFlag redmage:fire_camp
  * Keep carrying it. Take it home to her hearth when we pass Saltmoss. -> home
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag redmage:fire_home
  * Let it go out. You've carried her long enough. -> out
    do: AddTrust $with -3
    do: SetFlag redmage:fire_out

node campfire hero
  All of you. Yes. She always did cook for half the lane. Stand back, Commander. It's been waiting nine years, and it's going to be pleased with itself.

node home hero
  Home. Back where it came out of, with me carrying it, and you beside me, and that orb of yours in your pocket. Whatever happens at that hearth, it won't be cold. I'll feed it twice as much peat till then.

node out hero
  Let it go out. Maybe. Maybe that's what she'd say too. Not tonight, though. Tonight I'll just close the lid and leave it to decide for itself. Goodnight, Commander.
